{"call_id": "b054fd0cdcd345ddbdc07309a9f7fa41", "success": true, "result_file": "/data/nly/Agent-Aware-Trajectory-Level-Query/benchmark/fullbench/runs/fad/yelp/query3/full-01/results/b054fd0cdcd345ddbdc07309a9f7fa41.json", "row_count": null, "preview": "{\"submitted\": true, \"answer\": \"Answer: 35\\n\\nMethodology:\\n1. From user_database.review (DuckDB), parsed all 2,000 review dates (which appear in three mixed formats: \\\"YYYY-MM-DD HH:MM:SS\\\", \\\"DD Mon YYYY, HH:MM\\\", and \\\"Month DD, YYYY at HH:MM AM/PM\\\") and found 67 distinct businesses (business_ref) that received at least one review during calendar year 2018.\\n2. Mapped review.business_ref (\\\"businessref_N\\\") to business.business_id (\\\"businessid_N\\\") in businessinfo_database.business (MongoDB) by numeric suffix and fetched the attributes of those 67 businesses (all 67 found).\\n3. A business counts as offering parking if its attributes indicate either:\\n   - business parking: a BusinessParking dict with at least one of garage/street/validated/lot/valet = True, OR\\n   - bike parking: BikeParking = \\\"True\\\".\\n   (Businesses with a BusinessParking dict where all values are False/None, with BusinessParking = \\\"None\\\", or with no attributes were not counted as offering parking.)\\nResult: 35 of the 67 businesses reviewed in 2018 offered either business parking or bike parking.\\n\\nNote: under a looser interpretation that merely requires the BusinessParking attribute key to be present (even if all parking types are False), the count would be 40; the stricter and semantically correct reading of \\\"offered parking\\\" yields 35.\\n\"}", "truncated": false}
